# Recall — project rules

Read `CLAUDE.md` at repo root for the engineering map (catalog + seams). Product status is `FEATURES.md`. This is not a week-one MVP (~44k API, ~50k mobile).

## Golden rules

1. Never put provider API keys in the mobile app — backend `.env` only.
2. Use model aliases in app code: `free-chat`, `smart-chat`, `title-model`, `memory-model`. Alias → provider mapping lives in `apps/api/app/services/model_catalog.py` (LiteLLM calls via `gateways/litellm_gateway.py`).
3. Never send full chat history to the model — memory + recent window (~10–20 messages) only.
4. Topic, memory, todos, projects, and other post-turn work are best-effort jobs — must never block streaming. Enqueue from `services/chat/post_turn.py` via `core/jobs.py`.
5. No arbitrary code execution — render/highlight code only. The sole exception: HTML/CSS/JS preview in a sandboxed WebView (and chart/diagram rendering). Never run Python/shell/etc., and never run code outside that isolated WebView. The preview WebView needs a dev build (not Expo Go).
6. Validate all LLM structured outputs with Pydantic before DB writes.
7. Symbolic math is server-side SymPy only — mobile renders; it does not solve. See `docs/math.md`.

## Ownership (backend)

Migrate product domains into `modules/<domain>/`; each module owns API, service, persistence,
jobs, and tools. Shared infrastructure stays in `core/`, `gateways/`, and `repositories/` and
must not import product modules. Legacy `routers/` → `services/` remains valid until migrated.
No business logic in routers or compatibility imports.

New chat-loop code belongs in `apps/api/app/services/chat/`. Quota + prepare lock: `async with turn_resources(...)` in `stream.py`. New external IO belongs in `gateways/`. Migrated modules own their adapters and jobs; legacy adapters/jobs remain in `services/mcp/` and `background/handlers.py`. All adapters register through `gateways/mcp/`; all durable jobs use `core/jobs.py`, never the stream path.

## Mobile

- Product code belongs in `apps/mobile/features/<feature>/`; `app/` files are routes only
- Feature API slices use the shared request client and compose through `apps/mobile/lib/api.ts`
- Tokens in `expo-secure-store` only
- Screens stay dumb; logic in hooks (`useChat*`, `useMemoryActions`, auth context)
- Rich fences: `lib/fenceRegistry.ts` + `components/rich/RichFence.tsx`

## In scope (current)

Chat + memory, Learning projects/quizzes, todos/reminders, search, suggestions, attachments/RAG, calendar/Gmail, speech, image gen, web search, i18n, Pro, and rich rendering (markdown, math, geometry/graph, charts, Mermaid, chemistry, sandboxed HTML/JS). MCP tool loop is shipped and **on** (`mcp_tool_loop_enabled` defaults true). The legacy one-shot `mcp_tools_enabled` pre-stream round stays off.

## v1 non-goals

No multi-user, no execution of non-web code or execution outside the sandboxed preview WebView, no duplex voice, no arbitrary user MCP servers. Do not treat “no tools/agents” as a hard absence — the owned tool loop is on by default.

A **web client** exists at `apps/web` as slice 1 (login + chat SSE). Remaining web slices are deferred. Keep `lib/api.ts` the single mobile network boundary and rich-block rendering swappable so clients stay portable.
